I am attempting to add an additional layer of defense by splitting access to the `agent-vault` proxy an the external network across separate interfaces.  I am doing this by joining my `broker` container running `agent-vault` to 2 separate networks: `agent-network`, `external-network`.  Then i join the container running my agent harness to the `agent-network` only which effectively forces all network traffic through the broker.  But if the `agent-vault` opens both ports on `0.0.0.0` as it currently does, then the harness _could_ attempt to connect to the management port.  By splitting the listeners across interfaces i can ensure the agent harness container cannot even reach the management network let alone the port.

